  "note": "Poll on Tuesday 15 January 1929; twelve candidates for nine seats. The council became six Nationalists and three Unionists. The Irish Weekly prints Martin's vote as 221 (the Witness and the Armagh Guardian have 227) and names the Witness's \"James Moon\" as James Moore. Some Nationalist candidates were nominated by Unionists and some Unionists by Nationalists."
